      "message": "feat(sim): the hidden-rest scan answers past its holding budget\n\nPast the 1.2 M-cell / 40 M-claim budgets the hidden-rest scan read\nRestUnjudged (NOT JUDGED) and blocked the post. Those numbers now\nbound what the scan holds at once: a lattice that does not fit is\ncounted row by row, cut into row bands that do, and judged band by\nband through the same body, so the verdict is the whole-lattice\nverdict bit for bit. A new `work` budget (1 G visits + distances)\nbounds the whole walk; past it, or when one row alone cannot be held,\nthe scan still says NOT JUDGED by name. The nearest ball-center query\ngoes through an exact uniform XY grid (scan_near), ring walk bounded\nby XY ring distance and the path's Z gap.\n\nReading: a 21-plate stack, 1.07 M columns, 44.0 M claims (past the\nshipped 40 M): was NOT JUDGED, now judged 41.206 mm hidden rest;\nrelease 14.5 s (2.2 s without the hidden half).\n\nFixes #24\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
